Created by PLY version 3.11 (http://www.dabeaz.com/ply)

Unused terminals:

    COMMA
    ELSE
    EQ
    GE
    GT
    IF
    LBRACE
    LBRACKET
    LE
    LT
    NE
    RBRACE
    RBRACKET
    WHILE

Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> program
Rule 1     program -> statements
Rule 2     statements -> statement statements
Rule 3     statements -> statement
Rule 4     statement -> INT IDENTIFIER SEMICOLON
Rule 5     statement -> FLOAT IDENTIFIER SEMICOLON
Rule 6     statement -> IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression SEMICOLON
Rule 7     statement -> PRINT LPAREN IDENTIFIER RPAREN SEMICOLON
Rule 8     expression -> expression PLUS term
Rule 9     expression -> expression MINUS term
Rule 10    expression -> term
Rule 11    term -> term TIMES factor
Rule 12    term -> term DIVIDE factor
Rule 13    term -> factor
Rule 14    factor -> NUMBER
Rule 15    factor -> IDENTIFIER
Rule 16    factor -> LPAREN expression RPAREN

Terminals, with rules where they appear

ASSIGN               : 6
COMMA                : 
DIVIDE               : 12
ELSE                 : 
EQ                   : 
FLOAT                : 5
GE                   : 
GT                   : 
IDENTIFIER           : 4 5 6 7 15
IF                   : 
INT                  : 4
LBRACE               : 
LBRACKET             : 
LE                   : 
LPAREN               : 7 16
LT                   : 
MINUS                : 9
NE                   : 
NUMBER               : 14
PLUS                 : 8
PRINT                : 7
RBRACE               : 
RBRACKET             : 
RPAREN               : 7 16
SEMICOLON            : 4 5 6 7
TIMES                : 11
WHILE                : 
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

expression           : 6 8 9 16
factor               : 11 12 13
program              : 0
statement            : 2 3
statements           : 1 2
term                 : 8 9 10 11 12

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . program
    (1) program -> . statements
    (2) statements -> . statement statements
    (3) statements -> . statement
    (4) statement -> . INT IDENTIFIER SEMICOLON
    (5) statement -> . FLOAT IDENTIFIER SEMICOLON
    (6) statement -> . IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression SEMICOLON
    (7) statement -> . PRINT LPAREN IDENTIFIER RPAREN SEMICOLON

    INT             shift and go to state 4
    FLOAT           shift and go to state 6
    IDENTIFIER      shift and go to state 5
    PRINT           shift and go to state 7

    program                        shift and go to state 1
    statements                     shift and go to state 2
    statement                      shift and go to state 3

state 1

    (0) S' -> program .



state 2

    (1) program -> statements .

    $end            reduce using rule 1 (program -> statements .)


state 3

    (2) statements -> statement . statements
    (3) statements -> statement .
